# 14. Established Foundations vs. Proposed Contribution

The project should remain explicit about what is already established.

## Established

The following are established areas of mathematics, engineering, and decision science:

* Bayesian inference;
* state estimation;
* partially observable decision models;
* entropy;
* information gain;
* value-of-information analysis;
* dynamic systems;
* observability;
* feedback control;
* predictive control;
* human factors;
* human-in-the-loop systems.

## Proposed

The proposed contribution is the architectural integration of these concepts into a single reusable framework where:

```text
Evidence
+
Belief
+
Uncertainty
+
Information value
+
Time
+
Action
+
Human authority
+
Observed response
```

are represented as connected parts of the same system.

That is the claim to test.

It is not a claim that the underlying mathematics was invented here.

